  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_a85c9e6c1bcb43f4832d4728419d1620",
      "statement": "The Durable Object storage API is backed by per-cell SQLite: async in JS but synchronous underneath, with sync Rust ops wrapped in async by the JS harness, and each cell owning its own database file and epoch-fenced bucket prefix.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/storage.rs#L6-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:70efb51767a5944f51fe86cb6ba9c9e77e1d0b44753431b624eafda074c770a4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_96bf9d3535874c718e6b0c69f4feda29",
      "statement": "Cell storage state belongs to the isolate, not a thread, because a cell event's turns run on whatever tokio worker holds the isolate; no synchronization is needed because a turn holds the isolate lock.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/storage.rs#L22-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2e51a6e757a89997357e57c46af40a38d425b7923d2f828bd839d117261c9d12:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c4dde8a4ecd546b7aa436893e3124e20",
      "statement": "Each open cell couples its SQLite connection with the ownership epoch that authorized its activation, one residency invariant that prevents asynchronous work from recovering an epoch through a later ownership lookup after a takeover.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/storage.rs#L52-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0aee592c5655ca94f7a60d89cfe0c73b0d7f14485d7750992756f8a7017742ee:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7ff211f9186a4d5ab6238b58153678dd",
      "statement": "The storage ops surface converts V8 values to Rust, calls into storage, and converts the answer back; the storage semantics live in storage.rs and the value serialization format lives in storage_ops.rs because it is what JS can see.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js/storage_ops.rs#L3-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5ca4a3526d6627c2ba4cc1b3581dc46c41b918be8e3fd5132db5d566bdc53731:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_60c38f37f58141afa71d26e884df3211",
      "statement": "A schema cookie caches PRAGMA schema_version because the pragma takes a shared pager lock, and a handler that touches no storage would otherwise pay two locked reads per event.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/storage.rs#L62-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:beecdf1f9bd78a70d0af124b8fcabf6abbdc81f856489c65eca791910f8a1229:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bce189de689749ad9c794fd8509e2280",
      "statement": "A failed SQLite operation poisons the actor only when a critical engine error (SQLITE_FULL, SQLITE_IOERR, SQLITE_NOMEM, SQLITE_INTERRUPT) coincides with a destroyed transaction (autocommit re-enabled); anything else recovers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/sqlite.rs#L15-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef604ef62b0f43c0766fca3fd0f412c48cc1300ffbfd3c3dcddaeb5501ae2e76:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1cb38cf68a7a4ad28c9c3693e72db716",
      "statement": "A KV namespace is a cell (__KvNamespace) whose bounds ship as data the JS harness compares against; keys are at most 512 bytes, values 25 MiB, metadata 1 KiB, expiry below 60 s is refused, and a list page returns at most 1000 keys.",
